cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Forecasting the share of ICT specialists in employment in EU countries: replication code and data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Poroshyn
    given-names: Dmytro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9571-7829"
    affiliation: "Sumy State University"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dmytroporoshyn/eu-ict-employment-forecasting"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for forecasting the share of ICT specialists in total employment
  in the 27 EU countries for 2025-2029 and comparing statistical methods (ARIMA, ETS)
  with machine learning (Prophet, decision tree, random forest, XGBoost) and panel
  linear regressions. Scripts 01-15 reproduce the submitted manuscript; scripts 16-21
  reproduce the revised manuscript (multi-horizon backtesting, two-way cluster-robust
  tests, prediction intervals, employment-weighted EU aggregate).
keywords:
  - employment forecasting
  - ICT specialists
  - machine learning
  - ARIMA
  - XGBoost
  - random forest
  - panel data
  - multi-horizon evaluation
  - prediction intervals
  - European Union
